skimming of course for now. But the Sorcerer options in the Egyptian section, espcially with access to Sekhem, look quite intriguing, but my question is that the Mummy the Curse book is a world of darkness book and not a chronicles of darkness, does that make a difference?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>How can I know if what I claim I know to be true is rejecting the idea that there is something I might not know? How can I know if what I claim I don't know to be true is rejecting the idea that there is something I do know?<br /> -Zhuangzi","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1715-ostarion","name":"Ostarion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1715_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"305"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-23T06:47:07-07:00","id":1066824,"title":"","content":"I so regret not backing this Kickstarter when I had the chance, but I'm excited to see all the really cool content we're going to get. The splat sheet on the lost Promethean Lineage the Prophets is in the Black Death and/or Hundred Years War section, is it not? What are they like?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-23T06:49:07-07:00","id":1066827,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ostarion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1065560-dark-eras-companion-backer-pdf?p=1066822#post1066822\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, just skimming of course for now. But the Sorcerer options in the Egyptian section, espcially with access to Sekhem, look quite intriguing, but my question is that the Mummy the Curse book is a world of darkness book and not a chronicles of darkness, does that make a difference?</div> </div> </div> </div>No, Mummy the Curse is a 1st Edition Chronicles of Darkness book. The entire intellectual property has been renamed, not just the new edition.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-23T06:55:44-07:00","id":1066832,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1065560-dark-eras-companion-backer-pdf?p=1066827#post1066827\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No, Mummy the Curse is a 1st Edition Chronicles of Darkness book. The entire intellectual property has been renamed, not just the new edition.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm. But the books didn't change so they are still a New World of Darkness, not a CofD","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-23T06:58:45-07:00","id":1066834,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moinen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1065560-dark-eras-companion-backer-pdf?p=1066832#post1066832\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmm. But the books didn't change so they are still a New World of Darkness, not a CofD</div> </div> </div> </div>They say the words World of Darkness on the cover, but that is no longer the name of the intellectual property. Essentially, those titles now have errata.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-23T07:00:22-07:00","id":1066836,"title":"","content":"Okay, I really like the Mutapa empire because it challenges the presuppositions of the core mage book regarding whether or not the supernal realms (among other things) even exist much less are responsible for magical effects. This is something I did with other mages from various cultures but the example is extremely nice.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>How can I know if what I claim I know to be true is rejecting the idea that there is something I might not know? How can I know if what I claim I don't know to be true is rejecting the idea that there is something I do know?<br /> -Zhuangzi","edited":{"userid":1715,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1715-ostarion","user":"Ostarion","date":". 03-23-2017, 10:11 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1715-ostarion","name":"Ostarion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1715_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"305"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-23T07:05:25-07:00","id":1066841,"title":"","content":"Damn. And I thought it will be easier to discern them and talk about. oWoD -&gt; nWoD -&gt; CofD. But now when referring to nWoD I have to say CofD 1E <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> The confusion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":1747,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","user":"Moinen","date":". 03-23-2017, 10:12 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-23T07:08:36-07:00","id":1066844,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moinen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1065560-dark-eras-companion-backer-pdf?p=1066841#post1066841\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Damn. And I thought it will be easier to discern them and talk about. oWoD -&gt; nWoD -&gt; CofD. But now when referring to nWoD I have say CofD 1E <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> The confusion.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, there is no more &quot;classic&quot; and &quot;new&quot; World of Darkness. There's just World of Darkness and Chronicles of Darkness. That was kind of the point of the change.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-23T08:17:01-07:00","id":1066891,"title":"","content":"Hah! Loving Forsaken by Rome, really well-detailed, not near done with it yet but it looks great. I think it was niknik? Who did it? Either way, kudos to the writer.<br /> <br /> Even the statue of meteoric stone is based in reality.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 03-23-2017, 11:21 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-23T08:20:13-07:00","id":1066893,"title":"","content":"I really appreciate that both Roman-era chapters contained themselves to a specific period and region. Requiem for Rome is cool, but it is a pain in the ass to timeline because it is a far reaching, both geographically and temportally.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-23T10:14:49-07:00","id":1066978,"title":"","content":"So, contrary to my initial scan, there are some slight changes to Cachexy. It still follows the model set by 1e, but the language has been updated to account for Tilts, and voluntary Dramatic Failures. Still far more similar to the 1e version than I had been hoping for. The writeup is really the selling point though, and it's done less like the blog posts and more like the Clan writeups in the core book. It doesn't follow exactly the same formula - doesn't begin with &quot;Something Dead Approaches&quot;, talks about the Morbus in third person instead of second person, doesn't have a sequence of &quot;see the (example)&quot;. It <i>does</i> have a Once Upon a Midnight Darkly in the Bloodline Origins section, but I don't think it's a reference to Snow White, unless it's to an obscure older version I'm not familiar with. Actually, I can't quite identify what fairy tale it's alluding to. Maybe Cinderella?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-23T10:22:16-07:00","id":1066983,"title":"","content":"So still at the beginning section of &quot;The Fall of Isireion&quot; and they mention an event called &quot;The Great Diaspora&quot; but don't really go into detail on what it is. I'm not super familiar with Mummy and as of this post, have only read bits of the first chapter, but I am curious to know more.<br /> <br /> Does the corebook or any of the other books in the Mummy gameline explain what this event is and why it happened?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-23T10:36:51-07:00","id":1067000,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tasti man LH</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1065560-dark-eras-companion-backer-pdf?p=1066983#post1066983\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So still at the beginning section of &quot;The Fall of Isireion&quot; and they mention an event called &quot;The Great Diaspora&quot; but don't really go into detail on what it is. I'm not super familiar with Mummy and as of this post, have only read bits of the first chapter, but I am curious to know more.<br /> <br /> Does the corebook or any of the other books in the Mummy gameline explain what this event is and why it happened?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's been a little while since I read the pertinent sections in the Mummy supplements so I might be fuzzing details, but basically after one of the Sothic turns that saw a large number of the Arisen awaken in areas near the Egypt of the time, infighting, the effects of Sybaris of so many Deathless, etc resulted in a messy conflict. A decision was made to disperse their numbers to avoid that happening again.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-23T10:37:31-07:00","id":1067001,"title":"","content":"Basically, the Deathless more or less broke Egypt towards the end of the First Sothic Turn (it's implied that a couple hundred to a couple thousand gods tossing around earth-shaking magic with impunity in service to their own agendas more or less gutted Kemet and caused the First Intermediate Period) at which point the Guildmasters got together and collectively decided to ensure that this many Deathless were never packed into such a small geographic area ever again, and established laws governing what the Deathless could, or could not, do to each other or to mortal populations in the future. The Prince of Glass, signature character for the Sesha-Hebsu, was one of the architects of this plan and the Diasporic Code that is written in Guildhalls of the Deathless.<br /> <br /> The Diasporic Code is as follows<ul><li><b>The Heart Law: </b>&quot;Interfere with the cults of other Deathless if you would fertilize the sands with the blood of mortals under the gods' silent gaze.&quot;</li> <li><b>The Spirit Law: </b>&quot;When desires clash, submit to arbitration or suffer judgement.&quot;</li> <li><b>The Essence Law: </b>&quot;Do not break the seal of a holy tomb unless you wish to offer its treasures sevenfold.&quot;</li> <li><b>The Name Law: </b>&quot;Make no alliance with the Lifeless or usurper's of Irem's lore, or you will worship at the altar of 42 Torments.&quot;</li> <li><b>The Shadow Law: </b>&quot;Grasp the sunlit flail of rule and you shall be condemned to the dark sarcophagus.&quot;</li> </ul>Firstly, mess with your fellow Deathless and it will cause unnecessary mortal death and the irritating process of rebuilding a cult. If you <i>do </i>run into a situation where your interests and those of another Deathless One come into conflict, take it up with the Guilds or (preferably) go to the Scribes because that's their job anyways. Don't desecrate the dead, jerk. Besides, tombs are the closest thing to a home the Deathless have. If you betray the Guilds and the memory of Irem, especially to Sorcerers or servants of Ammut, then you're going to die. Painfully. Several times, probably. Most humans never experienced (or survived) each of the 42 Torments individually. Lastly, don't rule openly as a god-king. This makes things more complicated for your fellow Deathless, but more importantly it proves the existence of magic. If you learned how to wield it within your original mortal lifetime, <i>so can others</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-23T10:59:23-07:00","id":1067015,"title":"","content":"so- how good is the Black Death? It is the main reason I regret not backing Dark Eras beyond Hunter's chapters, so I need to know if it is justified or if I should lower my expectations.. <br /> <br /> Also- how are the immortals from the Cleopatran Egypt?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-23T11:27:17-07:00","id":1067034,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1065560-dark-eras-companion-backer-pdf?p=1067015#post1067015\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">so- how good is the Black Death? It is the main reason I regret not backing Dark Eras beyond Hunter's chapters, so I need to know if it is justified or if I should lower my expectations..</div> </div> </div> </div>I haven't finished reading it, but I am enjoying it a lot so far. Let down by the minimal changes to Morbus, but that hasn't ruined the setting for me. Actually while I was really hyped for the vampire part of the setting, I'm finding that the Promethean bits are the ones that are the most compelling. When human fragility is on such prominent display, the Pilgrimage becomes a very different prospect. Is it worth becoming human if you know you'll probably only get to live as one for a few months, and half of it will be spent suffering from this horrible plague? I'll let you know more when I finish, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 03-23-2017, 02:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-23T11:57:05-07:00","id":1067057,"title":"","content":"So, the Amirani are pretty cool. I'm not familiar with the story alluded to in their history, so I can't tell who their original Demiurge is. But basically, they're made from the bodies of people who died violent or otherwise traumatic deaths, and re-made with metal. They retain the memory of the last thoughts of their donors, and this is seems to be the source of their prophetic ability - having seen the tiniest glimpse of whatever awaits a human soul after death. They only have one Bestowment, and it allows them to burn themselves to trigger prophetic visions, mechanically reflected by an extra bonus for spending Willpower as long as the aggravated damage from the fire remains. Their torment is related to being able to see how things could be better, but being unable to make that vision a reality. Knowing the potential for good in humans but seeing them choose to act on the bad in themselves instead, or especially being able to see their own potential and being unable to live up to it, is what triggers it. While in torment, their bodies show the signs of how their donors died.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 03-23-2017, 02:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-23T12:03:30-07:00","id":1067065,"title":"","content":"The Gallows Post return, but in this Era they're less of a courier service and more of a thieves' guild. Their nickname in this Era is the Brigands, and they seem to be a loose alliance of pilgrims, merchants, and highwaymen. They get access to Carthian Law, refluffed as a sort of pirate's code or honor amongst thieves thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 03-23-2017, 03:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-23T12:10:01-07:00","id":1067074,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1065560-dark-eras-companion-backer-pdf?p=1067057#post1067057\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, the Amirani are pretty cool. I'm not familiar with the story alluded to in their history, so I can't tell who their original Demiurge is. But basically, they're made from the bodies of people who died violent or otherwise traumatic deaths, and re-made with metal. They retain the memory of the last thoughts of their donors, and this is seems to be the source of their prophetic ability - having seen the tiniest glimpse of whatever awaits a human soul after death. They only have one Bestowment, and it allows them to burn themselves to trigger prophetic visions, mechanically reflected by an extra bonus for spending Willpower as long as the aggravated damage from the fire remains. Their torment is related to being able to see how things could be better, but being unable to make that vision a reality. Knowing the potential for good in humans but seeing them choose to act on the bad in themselves instead, or especially being able to see their own potential and being unable to live up to it, is what triggers it. While in torment, their bodies show the signs of how their donors died.</div> </div> </div> </div> I'm pretty sure they can also take the Titan's Strength Bestowment.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-23T12:13:21-07:00","id":1067079,"title":"","content":"Huh. Roanoke offered a new type of Sin-Eater. I forget the term, but like the Stricken and Torn. The new one is the Pious, Death by Faith. Though I suppose 'old one' is more appropriate.<br /> <br /> That's where the Astraea come from. They're groups of Abmortals.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><img src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/wp-content/uploads/2017/01/Leblanc_Astraea.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 03-23-2017, 03:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-23T12:23:18-07:00","id":1067088,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar4418_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"4418\" data-vbnamecard=\"4418\">tasti man LH</a> may be happy to know that there is genuine crossover in Black Death - one of the example scenarios features a ghoul Alchemist (as in, the sort featured in the antagonists section of Promethean).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-23T12:30:37-07:00","id":1067094,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1065560-dark-eras-companion-backer-pdf?p=1066978#post1066978\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, contrary to my initial scan, there are some slight changes to Cachexy. It still follows the model set by 1e, but the language has been updated to account for Tilts, and voluntary Dramatic Failures. Still far more similar to the 1e version than I had been hoping for.</div> </div> </div> </div>The change to Contaminate, where it doesn't stop working after a single person touches the object, makes their abilities muuuuuch more useful.<br /> <br /> I was also hoping for a more thorough rebuild, but I'd actually forgotten how good Cachexy actually is compared to the other 1st ed bloodline disciplines.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-23T12:34:04-07:00","id":1067098,"title":"","content":"There is significantly less mention of the Strix than I had been anticipating.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-23T12:51:38-07:00","id":1067113,"title":"","content":"Love the Lodge of the Final Breath, and the Rhine Curse is so wicked. Curious if Larhndur is meant to be a Firstborn and what the Mothers were like.<br /> <br /> Well crafted. I never thought I'd be too interested in protectorates but these are great.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-23T13:23:39-07:00","id":1067134,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1065560-dark-eras-companion-backer-pdf?p=1067034#post1067034\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I haven't finished reading it, but I am enjoying it a lot so far. Let down by the minimal changes to Morbus, but that hasn't ruined the setting for me. Actually while I was really hyped for the vampire part of the setting, I'm finding that the Promethean bits are the ones that are the most compelling. When human fragility is on such prominent display, the Pilgrimage becomes a very different prospect. Is it worth becoming human if you know you'll probably only get to live as one for a few months, and half of it will be spent suffering from this horrible plague? I'll let you know more when I finish, though.</div> </div> </div> </div>I really love the idea of reframing a medieval Pilgrimage not as aspiring towards humanity (which is base, wicked, and sinful), but instead as a quest to acquire a soul. It's a minor change, but a brilliant one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-23T13:24:58-07:00","id":1067136,"title":"","content":"More upset than I should be that Magna Mater's name gets tossed around a lot in Forsaken By Rome but the text barely touches on her awesome cult, instead just using the name for an idigam.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-23T13:34:57-07:00","id":1067147,"title":"","content":"Roanoke seems to be a far more interesting Era than I believed it would be. Another reason to wait for the Companion's release :P<br /> <br /> Also, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar269_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"269\" data-vbnamecard=\"269\">Charlaquin</a>, I must say that this description of the Gallows Post sounds weirdly similar to the Wing of the Strangers from Requiem from Rome. Iv'e always wandered about the Collegia's finale fate- could it be that they survived in the form of the Post?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-23T13:45:31-07:00","id":1067153,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1065560-dark-eras-companion-backer-pdf?p=1067147#post1067147\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, <span class=\"b-bbcode-user js-bbcode-user\">Guest</span>, I must say that this description of the Gallows Post sounds weirdly similar to the Wing of the Strangers from Requiem from Rome. Iv'e always wandered about the Collegia's finale fate- could it be that they survived in the form of the Post?</div> </div> </div> </div>Possibly, though the Post seems to have an emphasis on travel, even in this incarnation, which the Collegia lacked.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-23T18:39:45-07:00","id":1067288,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1065560-dark-eras-companion-backer-pdf?p=1067088#post1067088\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar4418_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"4418\" data-vbnamecard=\"4418\">tasti man LH</a> may be happy to know that there is genuine crossover in Black Death - one of the example scenarios features a ghoul Alchemist (as in, the sort featured in the antagonists section of Promethean).</div> </div> </div> </div>Yaaaaaay<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1065560-dark-eras-companion-backer-pdf?p=1067098#post1067098\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There is significantly less mention of the Strix than I had been anticipating.</div> </div> </div> </div>On the one hand, with quite a bit of corpses available, you'd think that the Strix would be in a frenzy trying to snatch up as much as they can, since a few bodies of the tens of thousands stacked together wouldn't be noticed.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, maybe even the Strix have standards and would rather not inhabit bodies that are utterly ravaged and desiccated from disease. Bodies that would probably fall apart in a matter of days, if not hours.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-23T19:37:03-07:00","id":1067321,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1065560-dark-eras-companion-backer-pdf?p=1067079#post1067079\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Huh. Roanoke offered a new type of Sin-Eater. I forget the term, but like the Stricken and Torn. The new one is the Pious, Death by Faith. Though I suppose 'old one' is more appropriate.<br /> <br /> That's where the Astraea come from. They're groups of Abmortals.</div> </div> </div> </div>This makes me immeasurably happy, not just from the knowledge that this is a thing, but that we're getting a hint of what Sin Eaters will be like in 2e. I also can't wait to see what Changelings and Demons have on offer here.<br /> <br /> Also, it's probably the Doctor Who fan in me, but it fills me with an odd satisfaction to see so many aspects of history being written out here. Makes me want to GM &quot;A World Unmade&quot; from the Demon storyteller's guide...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5803,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","user":"Taidragon","date":". 03-23-2017, 11:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-23T19:55:45-07:00","id":1067329,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1065560-dark-eras-companion-backer-pdf?p=1067136#post1067136\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">More upset than I should be that Magna Mater's name gets tossed around a lot in Forsaken By Rome but the text barely touches on her awesome cult, instead just using the name for an idigam.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think there's something to be said about the idea that her cult is likely uninvolved with the Idigam living in the rock given the lack of mention. Or ideally that's the case. That might have crossed into uncomfortable territory otherwise.<br /> <br /> Of course, they might also be involved but in a very mundane way, just doing what they did anyway and occasionally doing things for the Idigam. I was leery of the idea that they might be pawns of the Idigam.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":159,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","user":"Leetsepeak","date":". 03-23-2017, 10:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-23T20:15:13-07:00","id":1067341,"title":"","content":"So I can't be the only one who caught the Abraham Lincoln: Vampire Hunter reference in &quot;A Fearful Lesson&quot; right?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-23T20:18:06-07:00","id":1067343,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1065560-dark-eras-companion-backer-pdf?p=1067341#post1067341\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So I can't be the only one who caught the Abraham Lincoln: Vampire Hunter reference in &quot;A Fearful Lesson&quot; right?</div> </div> </div> </div>I've actually never seen the film, but we have inside jokes about a lot of people being shit. Henry Clay was a vampire, for instance.<br /> <br /> What did you think of my intro fiction =D? True story, I wrote it on vacation in Las Vegas when my parents and sister were at the pool.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:12px\">-</span>","edited":{"userid":3093,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3093-hm8453a","user":"hm8453a","date":".  We in this context is historians, not OPP. 03-23-2017, 11:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3093-hm8453a","name":"hm8453a","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3093_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"636"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-23T20:30:12-07:00","id":1067354,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hm8453a</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1065560-dark-eras-companion-backer-pdf?p=1067343#post1067343\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I've actually never seen the film, but we have inside jokes about a lot of people being shit. Henry Clay was a vampire, for instance.<br /> <br /> What did you think of my intro fiction =D? True story, I wrote it on vacation in Las Vegas when my parents and sister were at the pool.</div> </div> </div> </div>I haven't read the intro fiction yet. I always skim the main parts for things that stand out, then I properly read the whole thing later.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-23T20:34:03-07:00","id":1067357,"title":"","content":"It doesn't help that clicking on an Era in the index skips you right past the fiction, I think. I forgot they even existed until I was done with Forsaken by Rome and wandered into whatever was after it. Thought about errata'ing it but not taking you to the topic seemed off too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 03-23-2017, 11:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-23T21:15:45-07:00","id":1067376,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taidragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1065560-dark-eras-companion-backer-pdf?p=1067321#post1067321\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I also can't wait to see what Changelings and Demons have on offer here.</div> </div> </div> </div>Unfortunately, there are no Changeling Eras in this book. And we've only got the one Demon Era in &quot;The Master's Tools&quot;, which covers the Russian Revolution of 1917.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-23T21:18:17-07:00","id":1067380,"title":"","content":"Rachel Judd wrote the Changelings section under Supernaturals in the Reconstruction Dark Era. I wrote Mages, Vampires, and Sin-Eaters.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:12px\">-</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3093-hm8453a","name":"hm8453a","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3093_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"636"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-23T21:26:24-07:00","id":1067386,"title":"","content":"Even if Changelings and Demons have less on-hand in the book, I'm still eager to see what it has to offer for all supernaturals. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-23T21:58:39-07:00","id":1067400,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hm8453a</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1065560-dark-eras-companion-backer-pdf?p=1067343#post1067343\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I've actually never seen the film, but we have inside jokes about a lot of people being shit. Henry Clay was a vampire, for instance.<br /> <br /> What did you think of my intro fiction =D? True story, I wrote it on vacation in Las Vegas when my parents and sister were at the pool.</div> </div> </div> </div>I really, really want to play that Alaskan plot hook in the setting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-23T22:23:17-07:00","id":1067412,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tasti man LH</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1065560-dark-eras-companion-backer-pdf?p=1067288#post1067288\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On the one hand, with quite a bit of corpses available, you'd think that the Strix would be in a frenzy trying to snatch up as much as they can, since a few bodies of the tens of thousands stacked together wouldn't be noticed.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, maybe even the Strix have standards and would rather not inhabit bodies that are utterly ravaged and desiccated from disease. Bodies that would probably fall apart in a matter of days, if not hours.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was referring more to the fact that they tend to be omens of impending disaster, and the plague was one of the biggest disasters in Europe. Also the mention in the core book of the Strix flocking in Romania during an outbreak of plague. If a smaller outbreak like that attracted them in large numbers, I would have thought the Black Death would have attracte even bigger parliments.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-24T04:28:47-07:00","id":1067494,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1065560-dark-eras-companion-backer-pdf?p=1067400#post1067400\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I really, really want to play that Alaskan plot hook in the setting.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yaaaaay!<br /> <br /> I promised children, didn't I?<br /> <br /> I wrote all six of those location based plot hooks. I love them all, but Alaska and Pennsylvania are pretty close to my heart. One of my undergrad professors made me go to the US Postal Museum, which I thought would be the most boring shit, but they had an exhibit that included information on KKK postal cancels, which I had never heard of before. I knew I had to do something with it, and it wasn't going to be &quot;wrote an article&quot;.<br /> <br /> There's also something about Louisiana that's just the right degree of surreal/off/horror IMO.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:12px\">-</span>","edited":{"userid":3093,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3093-hm8453a","user":"hm8453a","date":". 03-24-2017, 10:45 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3093-hm8453a","name":"hm8453a","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3093_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"636"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-24T07:44:58-07:00","id":1067584,"title":"","content":"Speaking of the Pennsylvania Story Hook, who wants to learn about KKK Fancy Cancels from the Curator of the National Postal Museum? Two minute sound recording:<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://soundcloud.com/nationalpostalmuseum/curator-calvin-mitchell-on-kkk-postal-cancels\" target=\"_blank\">https://soundcloud.com/nationalposta...postal-cancels</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:12px\">-</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3093-hm8453a","name":"hm8453a","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3093_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"636"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-24T10:15:28-07:00","id":1067663,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1065560-dark-eras-companion-backer-pdf?p=1067153#post1067153\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Possibly, though the Post seems to have an emphasis on travel, even in this incarnation, which the Collegia lacked.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well the Collegia was called, in full, the &quot;Peregrine Collegia&quot; (not that that is actual Latin or anything) or &quot;The College of Pilgrims&quot; so while it doesn't have quite the emphasis on travel as the later Post, it's definitely a viable assumption, if not directly stated, that the Gallows Post are the descendants of the Collegia. It is definitely something an ST could do in their games without creating an enormous dissonance. The thing about <i>Requiem for Rome </i>and the Camarilla is that the book focuses purely on the City of Rome and the Necropolis, so we only really see what's going on at the heart of all the roads, but it's implied that every major city in the Empire has their own Senex, Legionnaires, Cultists, and Collegiates. No reason to believe that, as the roads began to become more dangerous and the Empire fell apart, the Collegia took on the job of securing roads between domains.<br /> <br /> Though even 1346 is a millennium after the setting period of <i>Requiem for Rome</i>, so most of the people who would remember the Camarilla have likely either met Final Death or are in torpor.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12981-romulusgloriosus","name":"RomulusGloriosus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12981_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"342"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-24T10:29:08-07:00","id":1067668,"title":"","content":"If anyone is looking for extra Roman goodness, The 7th Edition Guide to Cthulhu Invictus recently crowdfunded through Kickstarter and should hopefully be out later this year. Even if you don't use the Mythos material, it should be nice for a broader history of Antonine Rome.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-24T14:34:42-07:00","id":1067792,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RomulusGloriosus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1065560-dark-eras-companion-backer-pdf?p=1067663#post1067663\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well the Collegia was called, in full, the &quot;Peregrine Collegia&quot; (not that that is actual Latin or anything) or &quot;The College of Pilgrims&quot; so while it doesn't have quite the emphasis on travel as the later Post, it's definitely a viable assumption, if not directly stated, that the Gallows Post are the descendants of the Collegia. It is definitely something an ST could do in their games without creating an enormous dissonance. The thing about <i>Requiem for Rome </i>and the Camarilla is that the book focuses purely on the City of Rome and the Necropolis, so we only really see what's going on at the heart of all the roads, but it's implied that every major city in the Empire has their own Senex, Legionnaires, Cultists, and Collegiates. No reason to believe that, as the roads began to become more dangerous and the Empire fell apart, the Collegia took on the job of securing roads between domains.<br /> <br /> Though even 1346 is a millennium after the setting period of <i>Requiem for Rome</i>, so most of the people who would remember the Camarilla have likely either met Final Death or are in torpor.</div> </div> </div> </div>I allways thought than the Carthian Law and Invictus Oaths should be inverse in a roman setting.<br /> The Senex were the Propinqui magistrates, the responsible of applying the Laws from the Forum, so it'd be logical they had a set of Law Merits to enforce those Laws.<br /> And the Collegia would had the Oaths, because that'd gave him unity and mutual loyalty so needed to mantain united against the Senex and the Legio.<br /> <br /> It'd be ironical if some archeologist Kindred world discover that. It'd be a terrible political coup against the &quot;pedigree&quot; of Invictus, showing the Carthisns as the true heirs of the Camarilla rulers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>LAND OF THE DAMNED: SPAIN (Spanish): </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/3MHWYm\" target=\"_blank\">Land of the Damned: Spain</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/52b0TX\" target=\"_blank\">Kingdoms of Blood: Spain</a>; Cities of the Damned: <a href=\"https://goo.gl/XFMSSe\" target=\"_blank\">Barcelona</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/AXxdgq\" target=\"_blank\">Valencia</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/zkI5a1\" target=\"_blank\">Carthian Constitution</a> (1812), <a href=\"https://goo.gl/5H8M4s\" target=\"_blank\">Three Arrows Pact</a>: <br /> <br /> <b>OTHERS (Spanish): </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/36HngB\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: The Redemption</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/6B9V8l\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Forgotten</a>","edited":{"userid":247,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/247-uxas","user":"Uxas","date":". 03-24-2017, 06:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/247-uxas","name":"Uxas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar247_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-25T21:38:48-07:00","id":1068173,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Uxas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1065560-dark-eras-companion-backer-pdf?p=1067792#post1067792\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I allways thought than the Carthian Law and Invictus Oaths should be inverse in a roman setting.<br /> The Senex were the Propinqui magistrates, the responsible of applying the Laws from the Forum, so it'd be logical they had a set of Law Merits to enforce those Laws.<br /> And the Collegia would had the Oaths, because that'd gave him unity and mutual loyalty so needed to mantain united against the Senex and the Legio.<br /> <br /> It'd be ironical if some archeologist Kindred world discover that. It'd be a terrible political coup against the &quot;pedigree&quot; of Invictus, showing the Carthisns as the true heirs of the Camarilla rulers.</div> </div> </div> </div>A historical revelation exacerbating ideological conflict among vampire society?<br /> <br /> Never would have expected that. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-26T00:12:46-07:00","id":1068206,"title":"","content":"So I hear that blood bathers have a update in this book. Can someone explain to me how they changed? Like are they similar to the minor supernatural template such as Ghoul or Wolf-Blooded, or like the Lost Boys or Physic Vampires from hurt lockers?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10820-blakemikizuki","name":"Blakemikizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10820_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"280"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-26T08:08:30-07:00","id":1068296,"title":"","content":"They're more like minor templates, but any human who performs one of the two described rituals becomes one without needing sponsorship from a major template or having to come from a bloodline tied to one either.<br /> However, the first style of Blood Bather requires Iremite symbols to be incorporated in the ritual and they become immune to Sybaris. That and their narrative ties to mummies makes them practically a minor template to MtC similar to wolf-blooded and WtF (except wolf-blooded can actually become werewolves).<br /> The other style has no explicit ties to mummies at all.<br /> There's no mention of being barred from Supernatural Merits or anything like that, and the two rituals described are just examples. Other rituals could exist with other types of benefits.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":11887,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","user":"Tessie","date":". 03-26-2017, 11:57 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-26T08:15:33-07:00","id":1068298,"title":"","content":"Hell, where are Blood Bathers? Cause I seems to missed them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-26T08:25:38-07:00","id":1068302,"title":"","content":"Page 44 to 47.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-29T12:24:52-07:00","id":1070232,"title":"","content":"Holy shit. There's a write-up of Adam in the Promethean era &quot;The Year Without Summer&quot;. I'm a bit busy these days, but can't wait to read this chapter. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> (I still want a modern write-up in a future Night Horrors for Promethean, though. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> )<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/196-max-deltree","name":"Max Deltree","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar196_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"178"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-29T17:39:11-07:00","id":1070401,"title":"","content":"Speaking of which I've noticed that out of all the Eras in DEC, mysteriously no one has really talked about &quot;The Year Without Summer&quot; at any length. That while all of the gameline specific Eras have their own threads, this one does not.<br /> <br /> I have yet to get to that Era myself since I'm (foolishly, apparently) reading the book in order, from cover to back and in the middle of Forsaken by Rome but...should I be worried?<br /> <br /> Last time I've seen something like this happen where, on a different site, there was a thread for the nu-Powerpuff Girls was airing and everyone stopped posting after...the twerking episode.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-29T18:05:05-07:00","id":1070410,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tasti man LH</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1065560-dark-eras-companion-backer-pdf?p=1070401#post1070401\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Speaking of which I've noticed that out of all the Eras in DEC, mysteriously no one has really talked about &amp;quot;The Year Without Summer&amp;quot; at any length. That while all of the gameline specific Eras have their own threads, this one does not.<br /> <br /> I have yet to get to that Era myself since I'm (foolishly, apparently) reading the book in order, from cover to back and in the middle of Forsaken by Rome but...should I be worried?<br /> <br /> Last time I've seen something like this happen where, on a different site, there was a thread for the nu-Powerpuff Girls was airing and everyone stopped posting after...the twerking episode.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nope. I made a lot of the initial threads based off of what I've read to date. Haven't got to A Year Without Summer yet and I suspect that's the case with others too. I'll note there is no thread for Lifting the Veil either, and while I haven't finished yet, I honestly think it is one of the best eras of the entire Kickstarter. From what I've simmer of YWS, it looks pretty awesome.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-29T18:54:19-07:00","id":1070425,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Second Chances</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1065560-dark-eras-companion-backer-pdf?p=1070410#post1070410\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nope. I made a lot of the initial threads based off of what I've read to date. Haven't got to A Year Without Summer yet and I suspect that's the case with others too. I'll note there is no thread for Lifting the Veil either, and while I haven't finished yet, I honestly think it is one of the best eras of the entire Kickstarter. From what I've simmer of YWS, it looks pretty awesome.</div> </div> </div> </div>Even then, I'm not sure what that says about the Era in that everyone is quick to run off and read through the other Eras before getting to this one.<br /> <br /> Although I suppose when you have the high-level concepts of each era be stuff like &quot;Russian Revolution of 1917&quot;, &quot;Black Death in Europe&quot;, &quot;Ancient Roman Empire w/ Werewolves&quot; versus &quot;a clash of the Romantic period and the birth of one of the default Promethean Lineages&quot;, the formers are going to win over the latter.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4418,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","user":"tasti man LH","date":". 03-29-2017, 09:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-29T19:11:57-07:00","id":1070433,"title":"","content":"I think everyone came into the book with certain interests. It's natural for people to go straight to them upon getting the book. Then there's the fact that not every backer is even on the forum. And, in my own views entirely without any factual numbers to look at, I think the forum's been less busy this week.<br /> <br /> It's interesting, I went back to see the Update for it to see what it was up against.<br /> <br /> Geist: The Roanoke Colony<br /> Promethean: Year Without a Summer (1816 Germany/Switzerland) - a volcanic eruption in 1815 led to a 1816 having no summer which caused famine and food riots in Europe. And in June 1816, Mary Shelley, Lord Byron, and John Polidori stayed indoors and told each other scary stories...<br /> Hunter: WWII in the Pacific<br /> Vampire: On the Orient Express - elegance and claustrophobia on the most romantic of pre-WW2 trains.<br /> Hunter: 1830s India - The Thuggee cult was active during that time.<br /> Geist: Haiti in the 1970s-80s - a la Serpent and the Rainbow.<br /> Vampire: Jazz Age Requiem - Prohibition and the Great Gatsby. With maybe a pinch of Miss Fisher's Murder Mysteries.<br /> <br /> Obviously Geist won the next round. It was at this point I think they were combining eras that had lost before and were just letting backers pick them off. The next stretch goal I think since Roanoke was the runner up, with Promethean only winning by 7 votes, they just automatically had it without a separate vote. Jazz Age Requiem was in a far third. I believe I voted for Hunter in the Pacific. I wanted vampire to win another one but it seemed clear they weren't going to for whatever reason.<br /> <br /> The next actual vote had all the failures, and Forsaken by Rome won narrowly against Book of Judges Hunter.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 03-29-2017, 10:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-29T19:19:25-07:00","id":1070438,"title":"","content":"After chewing on it for a good long while, I think I've settled on not liking A Year Without Summer. Historical fiction/fantasy that brings actual people into the mix has always felt sort of theme park tacky to me, and I feel like there are smoother ways to integrate Mary Shelley into a world with Frankenstein's Monsters than to actually have her make them herself. I'm also not super sure how to get something playable out of A Year Without Summer; it feels more like a useful bit of setting information than an actual world for my players to jump into.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-29T20:04:40-07:00","id":1070457,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1065560-dark-eras-companion-backer-pdf?p=1070438#post1070438\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">After chewing on it for a good long while, I think I've settled on not liking A Year Without Summer. Historical fiction/fantasy that brings actual people into the mix has always felt sort of theme park tacky to me, and I feel like there are smoother ways to integrate Mary Shelley into a world with Frankenstein's Monsters than to actually have her make them herself. I'm also not super sure how to get something playable out of A Year Without Summer; it feels more like a useful bit of setting information than an actual world for my players to jump into.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have noticed a lot more of this in DEC, which I haven't found tacky, but have found a bit jarring. If for no other reason than that I though CofD had been moving away from making historical figures into Supernatural agents. Right now I'm okay with it though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-29T20:21:37-07:00","id":1070461,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Second Chances</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1065560-dark-eras-companion-backer-pdf?p=1070457#post1070457\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have noticed a lot more of this in DEC, which I haven't found tacky, but have found a bit jarring. If for no other reason than that I though CofD had been moving away from making historical figures into Supernatural agents.</div> </div> </div> </div>For accountability's sake, don't forget that we made the Brothers Grimm a Changeling and a Fetch.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:12px\">-</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3093-hm8453a","name":"hm8453a","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3093_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"636"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-29T20:45:07-07:00","id":1070466,"title":"","content":"I like the Year Without Summer as a story... but I'm not sure I like it as a <i>setting</i> if that makes any sense. It feels like a completed story to me, I'm not sure how any game I'd run could add to it.<br /> <br /> That said, the Promethean sections are blowing me away, because it's adding more horrifying and beautiful stuff that's just <i>out there </i> that Promethean characters can get in to, and gives me a better idea of what Promethean NPCs do in their spare time, and what Athanors are like. I particularly liked the one with the eternal Firestorm, a Tammuz frozen in stasis by a qashmal to save her from falling off the Pilgrimage so she can take the final step and complete the New Dawn.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-29T20:57:27-07:00","id":1070469,"title":"","content":"Because I forgot to actually post it: the Amirani might be my favorite Lineage now, I'm in love with the Refinement of Pneuma (and would adore seeing other historical variants, failed or otherwise), and thought the bit on framing a medieval Pilgimage not as a quest for humanity for humanity's sake, but rather a journey towards a soul and oneness with God after death.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-30T03:39:59-07:00","id":1070553,"title":"","content":"I have mixed feelings about Year Without Summer. I mean, it's written well and I can see what the writers were aiming for but, I don't know, I was so convinced that Victor Frankenstein was a thing in the Chronicles of Darkness that the chapter just did not click for me. I am a little old-fashioned when it comes to the classics and while I would have accepted Mary being a part of the story as she is in many adaptations of Frankenstein, cutting out Victor for Polidori is something I did not like. Hell, I would have been more accepting of Mary being the Demiurge without John being a part of the story. Still not the best option if you ask me, but one I could metabolize better.<br /> <br /> The fact so much of the chapter is focused on Diodati and its aftermath and does not give as much informations and plot hooks about the era as other chapters is another point of contention for me.<br /> <br /> I know there's a sidebar that addresses this specific concern and nothing stops me from Frankenstein being real in my setting, but it's not the same thing, It's clearly a matter of personal preferences and I'm not saying that the chapter is bad or anything, merely that it is not what I hoped it would be. It has parts I like a lot, but still. Oh well, to each his own, you can't like everything.<br /> <br /> Sorry if this sounded like a grumpy comment, but that's how I feel about it","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/815620-cinder-s-comprehensive-collection-of-creations\" target=\"_blank\">Cinder's Comprehensive Collection of Creations</a> - Homebrew Hub<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1172470-cinder-writes-about-beast-the-primordial\" target=\"_blank\">I write about Beast: The Primordial a lot</a>","edited":{"userid":38,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","user":"Cinder","date":". 03-30-2017, 06:42 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","name":"Cinder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar38_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-30T05:57:41-07:00","id":1070595,"title":"","content":"What really irks me in the Year without a summer chapter is the assertion that <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">The Prophet lineage needs to be wiped out so that the Frankenstein lineage can Live.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/885-bwgustaf","name":"bwgustaf","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;ba